// Chromium RTP captures for W9 `router_fills_units` (docs/spec/webrtc.md). Each packet is
// one decrypted RTP packet as received: the original header and extension bytes, then the SRTP
// plaintext with any padding kept. Each capture also keeps Chromium's offer and the answer
// Chromium applied.
//
// Rig: chrome-headless-shell 156.0.8078.4 (Playwright chromium_headless_shell-1248), run as
// `--headless --no-sandbox --use-fake-device-for-media-stream --use-fake-ui-for-media-stream`
// against a page on http://127.0.0.1; the media runs over 127.0.0.1 too. The page takes a
// 1280x720 fake camera at 30 fps,
// calls addTransceiver(track, {direction: 'sendonly', sendEncodings}) and keeps only the
// capture's codec (H.264 packetization-mode=1) plus rtx in setCodecPreferences. It posts the
// offer to a str0m 0.26.0 answerer (commit 2ada76a, after the http-post example) patched to
// append header || plaintext as hex after each successful unprotect_rtp in Session::handle_rtp.
// The page adds x-google-start-bitrate=4000;x-google-min-bitrate=4000;
// x-google-max-bitrate=6000 to each non-rtx fmtp of the answer before applying it, because
// str0m sends no REMB and Chromium otherwise stays near 300 kbps and turns off the top
// encodings. Only the AV1 answer negotiates the Dependency Descriptor: with DD negotiated,
// Chromium leaves TID out of the VP8 payload descriptor. The host was loaded, so frame rates
// are low (3 to 20 fps); the frame contents and layer structure are unaffected. Each capture
// ran for 15 s and is cut to its first frames per SSRC; RTX (including libwebrtc's RTX
// probe padding) is dropped.
// vp8_simulcast: HeadlessChrome/156.0.8078.4, [{"rid": "q", "scaleResolutionDownBy": 4,
// "scalabilityMode": "L1T2"}, {"rid": "h", "scaleResolutionDownBy": 2, "scalabilityMode":
// "L1T2"}, {"rid": "f", "scalabilityMode": "L1T2"}].
// Media PT 96; SSRC 677056966 = rid f, 3525936532 = rid h, 3250886639 = rid q. Answer extmaps: 2
// abs-send-time; 3 urn:3gpp:video-orientation; 4
// http://www.ietf.org/id/draft-holmer-rmcat-transport-wide-cc-extensions-01; 9 sdes:mid; 10
// sdes:rtp-stream-id; 11 sdes:repaired-rtp-stream-id.
// The first 6 RTP timestamps of each SSRC, in arrival order: 39 packets, 18 timestamps. largest
// keyframe 5 packets; packets with a nonzero partition index in the whole capture: 0.
